{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Behold, your days draw near to die.</b> Moses said before the Holy One, blessed be He: with the word הן I praised You, as it is written: ״הן לה' אלהיך השמים ושמי השמים״ etc., and with the word הן You put me to death. He said to him: also with the word הן you called Me a merchant, as it is written: ״הן בני ישראל לא שמעו אלי״. Another interpretation: Moses said to Him: with הן I praised You, as Rashi explained, and with הן You decreed death upon me — why do You measure a bad measure in place of a good measure? The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: this too is a good measure, as it is written: ״הן צדיק בארץ ישולם״. And furthermore, in the World to Come I will elevate you in glory onto a throne of pearls, and I will set you as head over 55 myriad righteous ones, the numerical value of הן. Another interpretation: הן has no pair. How so? alef = one, tet = nine, that makes ten; bet = two, chet = eight, that makes ten; heh has no pair, and likewise nun has no pair. How so? yod = ten, tzadi = ninety, that makes one hundred; mem = forty, samekh = sixty, that makes one hundred; nun has no pair. And Moses has no pair, as it is written: ״ולא קם נביא עוד בישראל כמשה״, and therefore ״your days draw near to die״, ״and I have chosen you for My portion״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:39.121754035Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}